"""Miniature implementations and falsifiable observations for each taught unit."""
CASE_FOR_UNIT={2:5,3:1,4:12,5:9,6:4,7:8,8:9,9:12,10:8,11:5,12:1,13:12,14:5,15:10,16:8,17:9,18:12,19:9,20:1,21:1}
CODE={
2:('Python · examples/mechanisms.py','from mechanisms import capacity, amdahl\nprint(capacity())\nprint(amdahl(.8, 4))','The default assumptions yield 5787.04 average RPS, 28935.19 peak RPS, 81 nominal active instances at hypothetical tested capacity and utilization, and 82 for one-instance loss. This is a worksheet result, not a validated infrastructure deployment.'),
3:('Python · arithmetic model','cold = dict(dns=20, tcp=40, tls=40, request_and_work=55)\nassert sum(cold.values()) == 155\nwarm = dict(request_and_work=55)\nassert sum(warm.values()) == 55','The warm example removes only assumed reusable setup stages. Real protocol negotiation, caches, overlap, connection expiry, and distance change those inputs. This code does not open a socket or benchmark TLS.'),
4:('Pseudocode · bounded upload ownership','queue = bounded_queue(capacity=100)\nstart_workers(count=50)\nfor upload in arrivals:\n    reference = persist_upload_or_reject(upload)\n    queue.put_with_deadline(reference)\nworker():\n    while reference = queue.take():\n        try: process(reference)\n        finally: release_owned_resources()','The queue bounds waiting references and the worker count bounds active execution. Large bytes remain in storage. The durable job and rejection policy must account for a queue handoff failure; a process-local queue alone is not durable work acceptance.'),
5:('Python · injected collaborator','class RecordingGateway:\n    def __init__(self): self.calls = []\n    def charge(self, command):\n        self.calls.append(command)\n        return "uncertain"\n\ndef pay(command, gateway):\n    return gateway.charge(command)\n\ngateway = RecordingGateway()\nassert pay({"amount_minor":100,"currency":"USD"}, gateway) == "uncertain"','The collaborator is injected and its uncertain result remains explicit. A production service also validates the money and owns persistence and reconciliation; this small function isolates the dependency, not the entire payment system.'),
6:('Python · lifetime identities','singleton = object()\ndef new_scope(): return {"scoped": object()}\na, b = new_scope(), new_scope()\nassert a["scoped"] is a["scoped"]\nassert a["scoped"] is not b["scoped"]\nassert object() is not object()\nassert singleton is singleton','The identities model one process. Actual containers differ in registration, disposal, and scope behavior. A real request scope must clean up owned resources; storing its object in a singleton changes the lifetime and can be invalid.'),
7:('Pseudocode · module contract','place_order(command):\n    priced = catalog.quote(command.items)\n    reservation = inventory.reserve(command.items)\n    payment = payments.authorize(command.operation_id, priced.total)\n    return orders.record_outcomes(priced, reservation, payment)\n# Modules expose contracts; they do not update each other\'s private tables.','This orchestration does not make three remote services one atomic transaction. In a modular monolith some local updates may share a deliberately owned transaction; external effects still need a workflow and reconciliation.'),
8:('Python · keyset continuation','from mechanisms import keyset_page\nrows = [(1,1,"A"), (1,2,"B"), (2,3,"C")]\nassert keyset_page(rows, after=(1,1)) == rows[1:]','The ordered pair supplies a stable tie-breaker. A real cursor also needs query and tenant binding, validation, and a defined consistency policy. Keyset pagination does not create a snapshot of a changing dataset.'),
9:('Pseudocode · bytes and metadata','upload = create_authorized_upload(tenant, expected_size)\nobject = store_and_verify_bytes(upload)\nwith transaction():\n    insert_document(tenant, object.version, object.digest)\n    insert_processing_intent(object.version)\n# Orphan-byte cleanup handles incomplete metadata handoff.','The authoritative metadata references a verified immutable byte version. If metadata commit fails, cleanup reconciles orphan objects. Do not claim one local transaction atomically contains a separate object-storage upload.'),
10:('Python · conditional seat claim','from mechanisms import open_demo_store, claim_seat\ndb = open_demo_store()\ndb.execute("INSERT INTO seats VALUES (1,NULL)")\ndb.commit()\nassert claim_seat(db, 1, "A")\nassert not claim_seat(db, 1, "B")\ndb.close()','The conditional update owns the local invariant. The verification suite also uses two connections to one store. External payment and expiry must preserve reservation identity and need their own workflow contract.'),
11:('Python · ideal LRU','from mechanisms import LRU\ncache = LRU(3)\nfor key in "ABC": cache.put(key, key)\ncache.get("A")\nassert cache.put("D", "D") == ("B", "B")','The ideal LRU example is deterministic. Production engines can approximate policy, include byte limits, and treat expiration separately. Eviction behavior alone says nothing about source freshness or safe cache-aside population.'),
12:('Python · stable rendezvous mapping','from mechanisms import rendezvous\nfor key in range(1000):\n    old = rendezvous(key, ["A","B","C"])\n    new = rendezvous(key, ["A","B","C","D"])\n    assert old == new or new == "D"','Adding an owner moves only keys now won by that owner in this model. It does not transfer data, synchronize membership, or distribute one hot key. Those protocols and workload effects remain explicit design work.'),
13:('Python · source and attempt fencing','from mechanisms import Workflow\nrun = Workflow("file-version-2", epoch=8)\nassert not run.complete(7, "file-version-2", "old")\nassert not run.complete(8, "file-version-1", "wrong-input")\nassert run.complete(8, "file-version-2", "current")','The miniature checks local identity and epoch. Persisting it safely requires an atomic storage transition and output validation. Provenance must also record transformation versions and relevant source regions, not just an artifact name.'),
14:('Python · ordering models','from mechanisms import vector_relation, lamport_receive\nassert vector_relation([1,0], [0,1]) == "concurrent"\nassert vector_relation([1,0], [1,2]) == "before"\nassert lamport_receive(5, 9) == 10','The first pair has no componentwise causal dominance; the second does. A Lamport timestamp smaller than another is not sufficient to prove causality in reverse. These values do not establish a consensus decision or real-time register behavior.'),
15:('Pseudocode · three replicas, one partition','A,B,C contain committed index 8\npartition isolates old leader A\nB and C elect eligible B in term 5\nB appends index 9, term 5\nB and C durably replicate index 9\nRaft commit rule establishes committed prefix\nA cannot acknowledge a new quorum-committed write alone\nrejoin: A follows term 5 and repairs uncommitted suffix','This trace assumes non-Byzantine members, correct durable protocol state, and a fixed three-voter configuration. It is not a replacement for the full Raft election and log safety rules or a production consensus implementation.'),
16:('Python · duplicate delivery, one local effect','from mechanisms import open_demo_store, consume_local_event\ndb = open_demo_store()\nassert consume_local_event(db, "E1", "orders")\nassert not consume_local_event(db, "E1", "orders")\nassert db.execute("SELECT value FROM counters").fetchone()[0] == 1\ndb.close()','The event ID and local effect share a transaction. Replacing the counter with an external provider call invalidates this one-local-effect argument unless the external boundary has its own protocol.'),
17:('Python · retry amplification','attempts_per_layer = 3\nindependent_retry_layers = 4\nassert attempts_per_layer ** independent_retry_layers == 81','This is a worst-case attempt-count model for nested policies, not a measured outage. Bound retries end to end, propagate deadlines, protect goodput, and preserve stable identity for effects. Jitter alone does not reduce the total permitted attempts.'),
18:('Python · synthetic tenant policy','from mechanisms import permit_demo\nactor = {"tenant":"A", "active":True, "actions":["read"]}\nassert permit_demo(actor, {"tenant":"A"}, "read")\nassert not permit_demo(actor, {"tenant":"B"}, "read")','This is an authorization predicate, not an authentication implementation. Every enforcement point needs trustworthy identity and resource context. A correctly denied API cannot compensate for an unprotected object link or worker.'),
19:('Python · one trace accounting model','stages_ms = {"other":300, "pool_wait":4600, "query":100}\nassert sum(stages_ms.values()) == 5000\nassert stages_ms["pool_wait"] / sum(stages_ms.values()) == .92','The trace spends 92% of its elapsed time waiting for a pool. Compare population traces, saturation, and lock evidence before generalizing the cause. The arithmetic does not identify why the pool is full by itself.'),
20:('Pseudocode · safe release progression','add_compatible_schema_field()\ndeploy_mixed_version_safe_code()\nbackfill_with_bounded_progress()\nverify_old_and_new_readers()\nretire_old_readers()\nremove_obsolete_schema_only_when_safe()','Code rollback is safe only while its stored data and protocol assumptions still hold. Destructive contraction and external effects may need a forward repair instead. Include configuration, artifact identity, and runtime readiness in the release evidence.'),
21:('Python · fictional comparison','from mechanisms import cost_options\ntotals = {name:sum(parts.values()) for name,parts in cost_options().items()}\nassert totals == {"single":371, "replicated_app":551, "partitioned":1402}','These fictional monthly totals do not establish equivalent reliability or capacity. Filter infeasible architectures before cost ranking. The complete case studies show the latency, consistency, security, and recovery checks required alongside the arithmetic.')
}
